From 3e0583417142f9491d6eba18c4950e22c91c5197 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saulo Vallory <me@saulo.engineer>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 01:12:52 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] feat(grammar): parse #id, .class and :name shorthands
 anywhere in a tag

Implements MX decision 146 (the `:name` sugar):

- Tag-adjacent `:b` is a new `shorthand_name` node, a sibling of
  `shorthand_id` and `shorthand_class`. The three compose in any order
  (`<a.c:b>`, `<a#d:b.c>`, `<:b.c>`), so `<a:b>` is now tag `a` with a name
  shorthand instead of the tag `a:b`. The name shorthand no longer feeds
  the tag's base name, so `<input:email>` is classified as the void
  `input` and `</a>` closes `<a:b>`. A second tag-adjacent name is an error,
  like a second id.
- `#id`, `.class` and `:name` are also accepted in attribute position, in
  html and concise mode and inside concise `[ ]` groups: first, or after
  any attribute (`<input type="email" :email>`, `input x="1" #b .c :d`).
  They follow whitespace, `,` or `[`; `f(x).b=1` and `...spread` keep
  their Marko meaning. They use distinct external start tokens and are
  aliased to the same node names, so queries treat both positions alike.
- Attribute values end before whitespace followed by `.ident`, or by
  `:ident` with no open `?` (ADR rule 4). `x=a ? b : c` is unchanged;
  `x=a.b .c` is now value `a.b` plus class `c`. Only a conditional `?`
  counts as open: the `?` of `??` and of `?.` (not `?.5`) do not, so
  `x=a ?? b :c` and `x=a?.[0] :c` split. The rule is whitespace-based,
  newlines included: `x=foo\n  .bar()` is value `foo` plus class `bar`
  (keep a chain without the space or in parentheses).
- A tag variable is not an attribute: `<a/b :c>` keeps `:c` as the tag
  variable's type annotation.
- A value on the sugar (`:x=1`, `<input:x=1>`, attribute-position
  `#x=1`/`.x=1`) is a parse error. Named modifiers (`class:x`,
  `style:x`, `value:fn:=x`) and `:=` are unchanged.

Tag-adjacent shorthands carry the `shorthand` field; the <style>
dialect injections match only those, so `<style .scss>` (a class in
attribute position) stays CSS while `<style.scss>` is SCSS.

Version 0.3.0 (minor): package.json, tree-sitter.json, package-lock.json
and a CHANGELOG entry, written by hand in the `changeset version` format
because the configured @changesets/changelog-github needs a pushed commit
and a GitHub token.

highlights.scm captures `shorthand_name` as @label. The htmljs fixture
harness maps attribute-position shorthands to the attribute names
htmljs-parser reads over the same range; __tests__/mx-shorthand.test.mts
asserts trees for every form, the unchanged modifier forms, and the error
cases. The README documents the node and both whitespace/tag-var rules.

